course: dictionary
lesson: 6740
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «Omnibus» is a good example, so the clues around it matter.
explain: «We watched the Sunday omnibus of our favourite show.» The clues are watched, favourite show and the week's episodes together. So an omnibus can be a book or TV programme that puts several stories or episodes into one.
explain: «The passengers climbed onto the omnibus in the 1800s.» The clue is passengers, people who ride. So here omnibus means an old bus, pulled by horses. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Omnibus» can be a noun or an adjective.
fact: An omnibus can be a book or TV programme that puts several stories or episodes together in one.
fact: «Bus» is short for «omnibus», Latin for "for everyone", the name of big horse-drawn carriages for all passengers in the 1800s.
fact: Cutting a long word short like this is called clipping.
exercise: «We watched the Sunday omnibus of our favourite show.» What is an omnibus here? | A kind of cake | A horse-drawn bus | A park bench | *A book or TV programme with several episodes together
exercise: «Bus» is short for «omnibus». What is this kind of shortening called? | Rhyming | Chopping | *Clipping | Spelling
exercise: «The council passed an omnibus bill covering housing, schools and roads.» What does omnibus mean here? | Very small | Going on a long journey | *Covering many things at once | Made of glass
test: «The passengers climbed aboard the omnibus in the 1800s.» Which meaning fits? | *A horse-drawn bus for all passengers | A book of stories | A kind of shoe | A TV programme
test: Lily says omnibus always means a book. Is she right? | *No, it can also mean an old bus, a TV programme or something covering many things | Yes, it always means a book | No, it means a kind of cake | Yes, it always means a bus
exam: «The omnibus edition puts every story of the series into one big book.» What does omnibus mean in this sentence? | A short, quick story | A person who tells jokes | *A book that puts several stories together | A bus for many passengers
